<div class="main-title">Likutay Halachos &mdash; Choshen Mishpat II</div>
<div class="sub-title">Hilchos Shomer Sachar<br>[Laws of a Paid Guardian]</div>
<div class="sub-sub">And in it will be explained the matter of Chanukah</div>

<div class="halacha-title">Halacha 2 &mdash; Part B (&sect;&sect;5&ndash;10)</div>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;5</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of Chanukah &mdash; which is called after the inauguration of the Bais HaMikdash [chanukas haBais HaMikdash]. For the essential revelation of the Ratzon is through the Shalosh R&rsquo;galim [three pilgrimage festivals], which call and reveal the Ratzon. And the essential holiness of the Shalosh R&rsquo;galim is in the Bais HaMikdash, where they needed to go up for the festival, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Three times a year all your males shall appear before Hashem your G&ndash;d,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Devarim 16:16)</span>.</p>

<p>For there, in the Bais HaMikdash, were all the korbanos [offerings], regarding all of which it says &ldquo;for favor&rdquo; [l&rsquo;ratzon]. And this is the aspect of: &ldquo;the Kohanim in their service, and the Levi&rsquo;im on their platform, and Israel in their standing.&rdquo; The Kohanim and Levi&rsquo;im &mdash; this is the aspect of the light of chesed that is received through the yir&rsquo;ah. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For the staff of Aharon blossomed, for the house of Levi&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Bamidbar 17:23)</span> &mdash; as is written there.</p>

<p>And all of this is made through the revelation of the Ratzon, which is revealed through &ldquo;Israel in their standing&rdquo; [Yisroel b&rsquo;ma&rsquo;amadam] &mdash; for they were engaged in the Torah, in Ma&rsquo;aseh Beraishis [the account of Creation] and in Parshas Ha&rsquo;azinu. Which is the aspect of the revelation of the Ratzon &mdash; that they reveal that Hashem, blessed be He, created everything by His will in the six days of Creation. And this is the aspect of Ma&rsquo;aseh Beraishis that the men of the ma&rsquo;amad would read. And likewise Parshas Ha&rsquo;azinu also speaks essentially about emunah &mdash; that everything is according to His will, blessed be He &mdash; as it admonishes there: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Remember the days of old; consider the years of each generation,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Devarim 32:7)</span>. And it concludes there: <span class="verse">&ldquo;See now that I, I am He; I put to death and I bring to life,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;and none can rescue from My hand&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Devarim 32:39)</span>. That is, that everything is according to His will, blessed be He &mdash; whether for death or for life, etc.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the Even Sh&rsquo;siyah, which is in the Bais HaMikdash, which is Kodesh Kodashim &mdash; from which is the essential holiness of the Bais HaMikdash. For the Even Sh&rsquo;siyah, Kodesh Kodashim, is the aspect of the Ratzon of the R&rsquo;tzonos, ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin &mdash; where all the r&rsquo;tzonos are connected. For this is the aspect of what Yaakov took &mdash; the stones of the place and placed them around his head, and they were all incorporated into one stone, in the Even Sh&rsquo;siyah. For <span class="key-term">even</span> [stone] is the aspect of ratzon, the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;a whole stone &mdash; His will&rdquo;</span> [even sh&rsquo;laimah r&rsquo;tzono]. That is, he took all the r&rsquo;tzonos, which are the aspect of stones, as above, and incorporated them all in the Even Sh&rsquo;siyah, which is the aspect of the Ratzon of the R&rsquo;tzonos.</p>

<p>For Yaakov is the aspect of the light of the Ratzon, which is the aspect of &ldquo;elder and of uplifted countenance&rdquo; &mdash; the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;those who seek Your face &mdash; Yaakov&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 24:6)</span> &mdash; the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;and you shall honor the face of the elder&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Vayikra 19:32)</span> &mdash; the aspect of &ldquo;the beauty of Yaakov&rdquo; [shufreh d&rsquo;Yaakov].</p>

<p>And therefore when Yaakov awoke from his sleep and Yaakov vowed a vow &mdash; and the essential vow was: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And this stone,&rdquo;</span> etc., <span class="verse">&ldquo;shall be a house of G&ndash;d,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;Of all that You give me, I shall surely tithe to You&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 28:22)</span>. That is, he vowed to give tzedakah. For the essential revelation of the Ratzon, which is the essential holiness of the Even Sh&rsquo;siyah, the holiness of the Bais HaMikdash, is through tzedakah, as above.</p>

<p>It emerges that the essential Ratzon is revealed in the Bais HaMikdash, where is the ascent of all the tefillos, which are the revelation of the Ratzon. For tefillah is the opposite of nature &mdash; for nature compels thus, but tefillah changes nature and reveals that everything is according to His will, blessed be He, as Rabbainu of blessed memory wrote elsewhere (siman 9). And therefore there were in the Bais HaMikdash many miracles constantly, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Avos, chapter 5): &ldquo;Ten miracles were performed for our forefathers in the Bais HaMikdash.&rdquo; For the miracles are the opposite of nature, the aspect of the revelation of the Ratzon, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore the Bais HaMikdash is the place of yir&rsquo;ah, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;How awesome is this place,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 28:17)</span>. For the essential yir&rsquo;ah is made through the revelation of the Ratzon, as above. And this is the aspect of Chanukah, the aspect of the inauguration of the Bais HaMikdash. For then one draws the illumination of the Ratzon and subdues the wisdom of nature, as above &mdash; through which the Bais HaMikdash is inaugurated. For the essential drawing of holiness to the Bais HaMikdash is through the revelation of the Ratzon, which is revealed through the holy elders who add holy light each and every day as they age &mdash; and this is the aspect of the Chanukah light, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore the miracle of Chanukah was through the Kohanim. This is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And strangers shall stand and tend your flocks,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;and you shall be called the priests of Hashem,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Yeshayahu 61:5&ndash;6)</span> &mdash; which is accomplished through tzedakah, through which the Ratzon is revealed, which is the aspect of Chanukah, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;6</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the Chanukah light near the entrance [ner Chanukah samuch lapesach]. The entrance &mdash; this is the aspect of tzedakah, which widens all the openings, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall surely open&rdquo;</span> [pasoach tiftach]. And through this is the essential illumination of the Ratzon, through the holy elders &mdash; which is the aspect of the Chanukah light, as above. For through tzedakah, the forehead of the serpent is subdued &mdash; which draws sustenance from the elders of the generation who lack completeness. And then the illumination of the holy elders is revealed, through whom the Ratzon is revealed, as above. And this is the aspect of the Chanukah light near the entrance &mdash; for the illumination of the holy elders who reveal the Ratzon is through tzedakah, which is the aspect of &ldquo;You shall surely open,&rdquo; as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;7</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the oil of Chanukah. For oil is the aspect of ratzon, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;May he be pleasing to his brothers, and dip his foot in oil&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Devarim 33:24)</span>. And as Rashi explained on the verse: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the yoke shall be destroyed because of oil&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Yeshayahu 10:27)</span> &mdash; &ldquo;oil&rdquo; refers to Chizkiyahu HaMelech, who was pleasing to his generation like oil. That is, he was pleasant and desired by the generation like oil.</p>

<p>It emerges that oil is the aspect of ratzon. And the revelation of the Ratzon is through the aspect of the holy elder, as above &mdash; and this is the aspect of: &ldquo;Like the good oil upon the head, that descends upon the beard.&rdquo; For there the Ratzon is revealed &mdash; the aspect of oil &mdash; with the holy elder. And this is: &ldquo;the beard of Aharon&rdquo; specifically. For the essential aspect of the kehunah [priesthood], the aspect of Aharon HaKohen, is drawn through the Ratzon &mdash; through which yir&rsquo;ah is made, and through the yir&rsquo;ah the chesed flows, which is the aspect of the Kohen, the aspect of &ldquo;and you shall be called the priests of Hashem,&rdquo; as above.</p>

<p>And therefore on Chanukah, whose essential purpose is to subdue the wisdom of Yavan, which is the wisdom of nature, and to reveal the Ratzon &mdash; therefore its mitzvah is with oil, as above.</p>

<p>And see in Hilchos Chanukah that is included in Hilchos K&rsquo;lai HaYayin, Halacha 1, &sect;8 &mdash; there is also explained the matter of Chanukah based on the Torah teaching mentioned above. However, it is impossible for the bais hamidrash to be without a chiddush.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;8</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the laws of guardians [dinai shomrim] &mdash; that the Torah obligated the paid guardian [shomer sachar] for theft and loss, and from unavoidable circumstances [onsin] he is exempt. But the borrower [sho&rsquo;ail] is liable even for unavoidable circumstances.</p>

<p>For this is a great principle, and it is explained in our words many times: that all the losses and damages are drawn from the k&rsquo;lipos, which are the <span class="key-term">mazikay alma</span> [damaging forces of the world]. And all the k&rsquo;lipos and damaging forces of the world are drawn from the heresies [k&rsquo;firos] and the <span class="key-term">apikorsus</span>, which are the aspect of the sages of nature who deny the Ratzon. For heresy and apikorsus is the root of the Sitra Achara and the k&rsquo;lipos. For the yetzer hara is called &ldquo;a foreign god&rdquo; [ail acheir] &mdash; heresy &mdash; as is explained elsewhere.</p>

<p>And therefore the essential guarding from all damages is through emunas haratzon &mdash; that everything is according to His will, blessed be He, and there is no nature at all. Through this the heresies are driven away and all the k&rsquo;lipos and all the damaging forces of the world that are drawn from them are nullified. And through this one is guarded from all evil. And therefore the attribute of emunah is called &ldquo;guard&rdquo; [shamor], as is known. For the essential guarding is through emunah, which is the aspect of the Ratzon mentioned above &mdash; that is, to believe that everything is according to His will, blessed be He &mdash; through which is the essential guarding, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;9</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of theft, loss, and unavoidable circumstances &mdash; regarding which there are distinctions of law between the paid guardian and the borrower, as above. For these two types of damages that come from the blemish of the Ratzon, as above, are drawn, G&ndash;d forbid, according to the degree of the blemish of the Ratzon.</p>

<p>For it is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above that there is a distinction among the heretics. For there are heretics who are called the aspect of &ldquo;evil beasts&rdquo; [chayos ra&rsquo;os] &mdash; who are the heretics for their own pleasure. For they have pleasure from this, to hold onto their opinion and their falsehood, etc. But there is a heretic who is in the aspect of the forehead of the serpent &mdash; who is wicked and denies without any pleasure at all, etc.</p>

<p>And from these two types of heretics are drawn two types of damages: theft and loss, and unavoidable circumstances. For there are heretics who fell into their heresy through the many errors that the Evil Inclination misled them into, through the abundance of his desires &mdash; for he went from his youth after the stubbornness of his evil heart and did not strengthen himself to conquer his inclination and to subdue his desire. And because of the abundance of his desires, he went and was led astray from one opinion to another and from one reasoning to another, until he fell and was led astray into great heresy. But in truth, it was all because of the desires of this world &mdash; for the desires brought him to heresy and apikorsus, in order to be able to fulfill his evil desire, as most of the heretics were ensnared in their heresies only through this.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of theft and loss. For just as the thief comes through the tunnel in concealment and hiddenness and steals and damages the owner of the house, and likewise a loss comes through distraction &mdash; so too these heresies come through the thefts of the mind of the Evil Inclination, which steals and causes the loss of his da&rsquo;as through many deceptions and crookedness, until he is ensnared in the trap of apikorsus. And therefore from such heretics, the damaging forces of the world that cause thefts and losses truly draw sustenance &mdash; for from there is their root, as above. And these heretics are called &ldquo;evil beasts&rdquo; that deny the Ratzon, whose subjugation is through the holy sage who connects all the r&rsquo;tzonos to the root of the Ratzon, which is the aspect of the maitzach haratzon, the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin &mdash; where Moshe Rabbainu, peace be upon him, departed, etc. &mdash; see there, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above.</p>

<p>But there are heretics who are in the aspect of the forehead of the serpent &mdash; who are wicked and deny without any pleasure, who want to deny, G&ndash;d forbid, the root of the Ratzon, etc. And their subjugation is through tzedakah. For through tzedakah, the forehead of the serpent that draws sustenance from the elders of the generation who lack completeness is subdued, and the forehead of the Ratzon, which is the aspect of the holy elders, etc., is made dominant &mdash; see there.</p>

<p>And from these heretics who rebel deliberately [l&rsquo;hach&rsquo;is], who are in the aspect of the forehead of the serpent, from them are drawn robberies and murders, which are called unavoidable circumstances [onsin]. For it is like a violent man and a murderer and a robber who comes by force and oppresses openly. And &ldquo;the forehead of a brazen woman was his, without shame&rdquo; &mdash; for he introduces the apikorsus openly, without shame and without desires &mdash; he only brazens his face and his forehead like a dog against the Creator of all worlds, the Great and Sovereign One, the Root and Source of all worlds, the Will of all wills, the Hidden One of all hidden ones. And therefore from such heretics are drawn the aspect of robberies and murders, which are the aspect of unavoidable circumstances, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;10</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the sale of Yosef to Egypt, and all the dispute that was between him and his brothers. For all types of dispute are drawn from the blemish of the Ratzon &mdash; through not connecting all the r&rsquo;tzonos to the root of the Ratzon. For in truth, the essential dispute is the dispute of the Evil Inclination, which disputes against a person and wants to bring him down to the lowest depths, G&ndash;d forbid. And the essential Evil Inclination is the aspect of investigations and heresies, which is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Their heart was divided&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Hoshaia 10:2)</span> &mdash; as Rabbainu of blessed memory wrote in the discourse &ldquo;Vayasaiv Elokim&rdquo; (siman 62) &mdash; see there. And from there are drawn all the disputes in the world, all of which come from the aspect of the dispute of the Evil Inclination, whose root is the heresies, the blemish of the Ratzon.</p>

<p>For in truth, dispute is a blemish of the Ratzon. For the essential dispute is between the r&rsquo;tzonos &mdash; that this one&rsquo;s desire is thus and that one&rsquo;s desire is the opposite &mdash; and because of this a dispute is made, G&ndash;d forbid. And all of this is because they do not connect all the r&rsquo;tzonos to the root of the Ratzon, which is the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin, the aspect of Moshe. For the root of the dispute of the Sitra Achara &mdash; which are the sages of nature who deny the Ratzon, and this is the essential aspect of dispute, as above &mdash; their root is from the dispute within holiness, which is the dispute between the true tzadikim. And from there is drawn down the dispute of the Sitra Achara, which is the heresies of the sages of nature, as is explained elsewhere.</p>

<p>And the essential dispute between the tzadikim and the upright is because they do not connect all the r&rsquo;tzonos to the root of the Ratzon, which is ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin, the aspect of Moshe, as above. For in truth, the tzadikim and the upright &mdash; each and every one, his intention is desirable, for the sake of Heaven. And even so, certainly their opinions differ from one another, for it is impossible for their opinions to be completely alike. For no two people are alike, and just as people are different in their appearances, so are they different in their opinions. And therefore there must of necessity be differences among them in their opinions and their ways and their practices.</p>

<p>And from the day of the creation of the world, there have never yet been two tzadikim and truly upright people who were completely alike in all their movements &mdash; even though both of them walk in one path and draw sustenance from one rav. Even so, there are many distinctions in their opinions and their ways.</p>

<p>[continued:] And the rule is that the essential dispute is because of the variation of the r&rsquo;tzonos. And all of this is because they do not connect all the r&rsquo;tzonos to the root of the Ratzon, which is the Ratzon of the R&rsquo;tzonos. For in truth, one should know that all the r&rsquo;tzonos of all people &mdash; even though there are great differences among them &mdash; nevertheless all are drawn from the Supernal Ratzon, in which there is no variation, which is the aspect of the Ratzon of the R&rsquo;tzonos, ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin.</p>

<p>And one who knows and believes this in completeness, certainly will not hold onto a dispute. For he will judge his fellow favorably always. For he will say in his heart: even though I know in myself that my intention is for the sake of Heaven, to complete this mitzvah and these Heavenly desires in truth, and my fellow prevents me from this &mdash; even so, his intention is also for the sake of Heaven. For he has a different opinion, and it seems to him that this is not a mitzvah at all, or one needs to engage in another mitzvah that is greater than this according to his opinion. And even though I am very firm in my opinion and I have true proofs and demonstrations that one must hold more to this path and to this mitzvah &mdash; even so, even if the truth is according to my opinion, who knows from what root my fellow is drawn? Perhaps according to the root of his soul he needs to conduct himself in a different way. For in truth, all the opinions and r&rsquo;tzonos are drawn from the Supernal Ratzon &mdash; only it is impossible to understand this.</p>

<p>And if each person would say this in his heart, certainly the dispute would be nullified. For the essential dispute is because they do not connect all the r&rsquo;tzonos to the Supernal Ratzon &mdash; where all is one, and where all is peace, for everything is included in one. And therefore the essential peace is through the Tzaddik of the generation, the greatest in stature, who is in the aspect of Moshe, whose soul is from the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin, the Ratzon of the R&rsquo;tzonos. For he knows the ratzon of each and every one, from where it is drawn. And therefore he is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;a man in whom there is spirit&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Bamidbar 27:18)</span> &mdash; who knows how to walk toward the spirit of each and every one. For he knows the spirit and the ratzon of each and every one, and he knows how to connect and unify the spirit and the ratzon of each and every one to the root of the Ratzon. And there he unifies and connects all of them in one Supernal Ratzon. And then great and wondrous love and peace are drawn among them &mdash; since all of them, in their opinions and their r&rsquo;tzonos, are connected and unified in the root of the Ratzon.</p>

